{key: D#m}
{tempo: 108}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The flood swept them [C#]away without a [D#m]sound
They knew nothing of [C#]what was coming a[D#m]round
So it will be when the [C#]Son of Man ar[D#m]rives
[F#]Taking one and leav[C#]ing the other a[D#m]live
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Do you know the [C#]day that your Lord ap[D#m]pears?
Or the hour of [C#]night that no one [D#m]hears?
If [B]the owner knew the [C#]thief would come
[D#m]He would keep watch to [A#]guard the whole [D#m]world
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
So stay awake because [C#]the time is [D#m]near
Be ready for the moment [C#]that you [D#m]fear
[B]The Son of Man [F#]comes at an un[C#]expected [D#m]hour
[C#]Keep your eyes [B]open, [C#]stay in [D#m]power
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Two men in the [C#]field, one is tak[D#m]en
